# The Dockerfile copies exactly what it builds — CMakeLists.txt, src, go.mod, go.sum, cmd,
# internal, and the UI sources — so everything else is context the daemon transfers and never
# reads.
#
# `build/` and the node_modules trees are the ones that matter: each is an order of magnitude
# larger than the source, and `build/` also carries a host-toolchain CMake cache that would be
# actively wrong inside the image if anything ever copied it.
.git
.cache
build
node_modules
ui/node_modules
ui/app/node_modules
ui/prototype
# The image builds the app itself, in its own stage. Excluding a local build here is what keeps a
# stale `npm run build` on somebody's laptop from being what ships.
ui/app/dist
docs
legacy
testing
scripts
deployment
*.md
*.db
compile_commands.json
Dockerfile*
Makefile
LICENSE
